# Intent: Fixes to the cloudtest image kind found by its first run on the unit (the vendor check failed at TLS and the host link never came up). Causes: (1) the normal and the test image carry no public root certificates on purpose (the bundle is a placeholder and ISRG Root X1), so the vendor's certificate chain could not be verified: the cloudtest kind now adds IDF's full list of standard roots through a new late defaults file read after the core trim (sdkconfig.cloudtest.late.defaults, copied to sdkconfig.late.defaults only for this kind; no other kind has public roots); (2) the vendor check ran in the activation task before the protocol was created, with up to 10 retries growing to 80 s, so the host link waited behind a check that could not succeed, and the single websocket client had been pointed at the vendor namespace only: the check now has 3 tries and waits (up to 60 s) for a real clock before asking, because the unit gets its time from the host and the vendor certificate has dates; the websocket client reads the vendor's address only when the hosted route has stored one and otherwise the paired host's (one link at a time, never both); (3) bench-visible lines: "CLOUDTEST check waits for the clock (year N)", "CLOUDTEST check starts: clock_year=N", "CLOUDTEST link: namespace=... route=... clock_year=..." at every connect, and self.brain.status now answers clock_year and link_ns. No time server is contacted: the clock comes from the host.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: main/application.cc and protocols/websocket_protocol.cc of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT); firmware/CMakeLists.txt, main/hal/maipai_cloudtest.cc and .h, main/hal/maipai_hosted.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: only after the owner's yes (docs/plan/cloud-brain-firmware-test.md): the log shows the clock year and the link namespace; with the host link up the clock is set and the vendor check starts after it; the vendor certificate verifies; if the vendor is unreachable the host link still connects after at most 3 tries; self.brain.status answers clock_year and link_ns.
# Kconfig: none (CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_DEFAULT_FULL is set only by the cloudtest late defaults)
# Memory cost: none in any other kind. In the cloudtest kind about 68 KB of flash for the certificate bundle and no internal RAM beyond the stock TLS buffers.

diff --git a/firmware/CMakeLists.txt b/firmware/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/firmware/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/firmware/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -55,6 +55,11 @@ if(EXISTS "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/sdkconfig.core.defaults")
     endif()
 endif()
 
+# Patch SF99: an image kind may override the core trim with sdkconfig.late.defaults, read after it (only the cloud brain test kind has one: it adds the public roots).
+if(EXISTS "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/sdkconfig.late.defaults")
+    list(APPEND SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/sdkconfig.late.defaults")
+endif()
+
 # Travel with the private network (patch TN01): scripts/fw-tailnet.sh downloads the pinned client into a folder outside
 # this tree and fw-env.sh names it. Without the variable nothing about it is built.
 if(DEFINED ENV{MAIPAI_MICROLINK_DIR} AND NOT "$ENV{MAIPAI_MICROLINK_DIR}" STREQUAL "")
